  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 206</b></color></size>

    <b>Padmapani, Ajanta Cave 1</b>

    <size=74%>Late 5th century CE

    <i>Mineral pigments on plaster</i>

    In situ, Ajanta Caves, Maharashtra (UNESCO World Heritage Site)</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    About thirty Buddhist caves were cut into a horseshoe-shaped cliff at Ajanta between the 2nd century BCE and the late 5th century CE. This bodhisattva of compassion, holding a lotus, is one of the most celebrated wall paintings of Cave 1.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Unknown authorUnknown author / Public domain / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>'
